          "type": "text",
          "text": "## Findings\n- In the chorus (bars 25–40), both pad tracks are active with the lead. **Pad Wide** is −12.2 LUFS / −10.8 dB RMS and **Pad Layer** is −13.0 LUFS / −11.5 dB RMS, while the **Lead** is only −22.2 LUFS / −20.6 dB RMS.\n- The pads substantially outweigh the lead in its core range: Pad Wide measures −12 dBFS and Pad Layer −12.5 dBFS in 400 Hz–2 kHz; the Lead is −22 dBFS there.\n- The two pad MIDI parts double the same chord tones in adjacent registers: at beat 0, Pad Wide has B2–F#3–D4–F#4 and Pad Layer has B3–F#4–D5. This stacks F#4 exactly and reinforces the chord midrange.\n- The master chorus render is −11.2 LUFS with 2.2 dB average limiter gain reduction; the dense pad balance is likely making the chorus feel compressed before the lead can establish itself.\n\n## Proposal\n1. **Pad Wide › mixer volume:** change **0 dB → −4 dB**.\n2. **Pad Layer › mixer volume:** change **−1.5 dB → −4.5 dB**.\n3. **Lead › mixer volume:** change **−9.5 dB → −5.5 dB**.",
